# Three frames deep. The arrow of `keepLater` is pushed to a list: it goes to a callee out of sight, which may keep it and what it holds, so `g` does not count as only called. That goes up: the arrow of `middle` is handed to a place that is not only called, so `f` is not either. All three arrows are made in the heap by their makers, and nothing is moved. (The mover that takes along what a closure holds has its native tests.)
# f1 = keepLater, f2 = middle, f4 = maker, f3 = deep
# -- source: closure-that-is-moved-takes-along-the-closures-of-frames-that-it-holds.ts
